nd explosives a lot  of the time it's pretty common for  villains to use those methods so it's  not that exciting he isn't the best at  hand-to-hand combat Harley Quinn on the  other hand has some amazing me lay  skills and it is a lot to do with her  background she was trained as a gymnast  and Acrobat according to Batman the  Animated Series she was an Olympic level  gymnast this makes her great in a fight  and fun to watch No  wondered the Joker needed her as a  sidekick she is also totally ruthless in  a different way from the Joker just  remember the way she cut out the  Enchantress's heart in Suicide Squad  they're mad fighting skills are what  make the Joker and Harley Quinn such an  unstoppable team  unfortunately it seems like the Joker  tends to overshadow Harley as the main  fighter she isn't appreciated enough  cooler weapons on a similar note Harley  Quinn uses way cooler weapons than the  Joker the Joker originally used jokester  weapons like buzzers and razor cards  that was unique but it wasn't very  effective as his character developed we  saw him using more and more common  weapons but let's face it guns and  explosives are overdone then there's  Harvey Harley's iconic weapon is a giant  hammer its cartoonishly huge which makes  it extra awesome to see the tiny female  villain wielding it plus the hammer is  usually themed to match her outfit even  when she is taken down the good guys she  has a sense of style the hammer has  changed a lot throughout the years but  it's part of Harley's character she also  has pet hyenas that help her out in a  fight they're both adorable and  terrifying Harley Quinn doesn't get  nearly enough credit for her weapons but  she is resourceful and might lease a  very extra giant hammers and hyenas make  a bold statement of course the statement  it makes is that Harley's bonkers  awesome aesthetic when you picture the  Joker you probably come up with a pretty  standard image it doesn't matter which  version of the Joker you think of he  pretty much always has green hair a  purple suit and a creepy painted clown  face his aesthetic hasn't changed much  over the years but then there's Harley  Quinn unlike many beloved characters  that no one seems to mind when her  costume changes she started out looking  like a court jester  she wore red and black outfit and a  jester hat later we got to know her with  the pale blonde pigtails with pink and  blue tips her red and black outfit has  had many versions over the years it's  been a full body suit and a crop top  there have been short shorts and a  corset the latest live-action versions  have her wearing a red and white t-shirt  that says daddy's little monster she may  be a villain but she always has a sense  of style she doesn't need the same  Universal costume to be iconic the same  can't be said about the Joker  what he died for me loves fiercely we're  gonna be perfectly honest the Joker  doesn't deserve Harley Quinn here's the  thing about the Joker  he doesn't love anyone but himself if he  did he wouldn't treat his most loyal  companions so terribly many people have  suggested that he's sort of in love with  Batman but it's more of a creepy  obsession than love and the Suicide  Squad tried to make him out to love  Harley but the rest of DC cannon just  doesn't support that he thinks of her as  a possession or a minion on the other  hand Harley Quinn loves him fiercely she  puts her entire career and life on the  line to break him out of prison and she  shows repeatedly how much she loves him  she wants attention from him she listens  to him and comforts him when he's sad  she's the only person that has ever seen  him cry but he doesn't ever return those  basic signs of love Harley also loves  her friends deeply - she's no sociopath  she feels real love for the people in  her life independent woman Harley Quinn  does not get nearly enough credit for  her independence of course she doesn't  start out that way  Harley was essentially the Joker's  criminal prodigy but he treated her like  a minion he constantly bossed her around  and she did what he said for a while but  then Harley became her own person she  made friends with Catwoman and poison  ivy she's stopped putting up with all  the Joker's mean antics toward her  eventually she became a criminal in her  own right and she was really good at it  she got a solo series of really popular  comics and she's going to be in the new  birds of prey movie she doesn't need to  star alongside Joker anymore Harley  Quinn becomes the leader of an awesome  group of antihero women who save a young  girl the fact that she has gained so  much independence from the Joker is a  big deal honestly we never expected it  there's a lot more to Harley Quinn than  we ever knew do not say this oath  topless Lee  full of joy The Joker might release a  constant demented laugh he might play  jokes and have a carefree attitude about  his criminal activities but he's not  actually happy he's a pretty troubled  soul who is solely motivated by hatred  and a desire for violence Harley Quinn  is a completely different story  she is troubled too but she has a  distinct joy in her life  in fact the writers of DC say that  giddiness is what makes Harley Quinn who  she is  anyone that can pull off her girlish  excitement can do the character of  justice  she loves fighting and committing crimes  she doesn't just laugh because she's a  criminal  she laughs because she's enjoying  herself she's a wild and carefree soul  her insanity does not derive from the  fact that she's a monster is that she  has an off-the-wall loopy sense of humor  you can see it in her pet names for the  Joker like when she calls him puddin  it's in her choice of clothes and in her  big wild eyes and it's always in her  laughs more relationships the Joker  doesn't respect Harley Quinn but he is  weirdly codependent on her it's part of  what makes their relationship so  unhealthy in certain versions the Joker  has confided in her even as he treats  her terribly she's even tried to end her  life on more than one occasion Harley  has an unhealthy love for the Joker it  may be her defining relationship but  it's far from her only important  relationship  Harley forms a close-knit relationship  with poison ivy their friendship is deep  and real poison ivy is an important part  of helping Harley Quinn gain her  independence  eventually poison ivy and Harley became  more than friends for a little while at  least  Harley also befriends Catwoman who helps  her see that the Joker isn't always the  best boyfriend she has also had a  relationship with Deadshot although it  got creepy very quickly in some series  she even becomes friends with Batman and  seems to care about him her  relationships are more interesting than  the Joker's he is never really seen  having a relationship with anyone else  it just goes back to how much love  Harley has for the people in her life  character growth if there's one thing we  can count on from the Joker  it's that he'll always be the same he's  always mad and he's always obsessed with  Batman but he never changes in any  version of the DC Universe character  growth is what makes characters  interesting and Harley has so much  character growth it's hard to keep up  with she grows from a rigid lonely  psyche  hydrous to a carefree criminal she  starts out being bossed around  but then learns to stand up for herself  she gains her independence and makes her  own decisions and then she almost  becomes a hero in the live-action movies  we can't wait to see her to roasts and  birds of prey certain things about her  don't change like her feelings for the  Joker and her girlish excitement but  that's what makes her who she is  Harley has changed a lot and grown into  an even more exciting character it's  part of her appeal and it puts her on  the same level as the Joker  not all bad the Joker is purely evil he  exists solely to cause torment in Gotham  City and beyond she has never shown a  good side other than rescuing Harley and  Suicide Squad but even that was for  selfish reasons Harley on the other hand  does have a good side in the animated  series she ends up working for Batman  you can't be completely evil and work  for Batman she even comes to respect him  and they become friends Harley makes  conscious decisions to commit crimes but  even she has a moral code she won't  cross she won't hurt the people she  cares about like poison ivy she has a  sense of justice even if it is warped  but the Joker doesn't have any of these  tricks Harley has also been shown to  have regret for some of her actions  that's another thing we would never see  from the Joker  she's been flat out kind before and we  expect to see more of that in birds of  prey for more videos about the hottest  Hollywood characters be sure to  subscribe to the things don't want to  miss another video well you can get  notified about every new upload when you  subscribe to the things and click the  notifications bell check your  notification settings if you're watching  on your phone that's a wrap  witch villain do you like better Harley  Quinn or the Joker tell us in the  comments thanks for watching  show your love for Harley Quinn by  hitting the thumbs up button see you  next time  you

